<%- include('partials/top') %>
<div class="wrap narrow doc">
  <h1>Seller terms</h1>
  <p class="muted">These terms apply to everyone who sells on EasyNotes, an independent South African business. Questions? Email <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>.</p>

  <h2>Eligibility and verification</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You must have completed a degree at a recognised institution and provide your degree certificate or academic transcript and your ID.</li>
    <li>We may approve, decline or withdraw verification at our discretion. If verification is withdrawn, your notes are hidden from sale.</li>
    <li>Once verified, you may add further qualifications, including honours, master’s or doctoral study you are still completing. Each is checked before it is shown.</li>
    <li>Everything shown on your storefront must be accurate, including your qualifications, institutions, dates, marks and any distinction. Claiming results you did not achieve is grounds for removing your verification.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your notes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Notes must be PDF files and must match their title and description.</li>
    <li>You give EasyNotes a licence to host and display your listing, show a preview of the first pages, and deliver your files to buyers. You keep ownership of your notes.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Original work only</h2>
  <p>Each time you upload notes, you promise (warrant) that:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>you wrote them yourself and own all rights needed to sell them;</li>
    <li>they don’t contain, in full, in part or as photos or screenshots, any lecture slides, lecturer notes or handouts; pages or passages from textbooks, study guides or course packs; past exam papers, class tests or memos; assignment, tutorial or test answers given out by an institution; or material from an institution’s learning platform;</li>
    <li>selling them doesn’t break your institution’s rules or anyone else’s rights, including copyright and privacy (no other students’ personal information).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Uploads are checked automatically for signs of copied material, and we may review any listing at any time.</p>

  <h2>If notes break these terms</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We may remove listings, hide your storefront, suspend or close your account, and withdraw verification, at any time and without notice.</li>
    <li>We act on copyright complaints as described on our <a href="/copyright">copyright and takedown page</a>. We may share your name and contact details with a rights holder who makes a well-founded complaint about your notes.</li>
    <li>We close the accounts of sellers who repeatedly infringe.</li>
    <li>If we refund buyers because notes broke these terms, we may recover those amounts by withholding them from your future earnings, or ask you to repay them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Indemnity</h2>
  <p>You agree to compensate (indemnify) EasyNotes, and anyone who runs it, for any claim, loss, damages, legal costs or refunds that arise because notes you uploaded broke these terms or infringed someone else’s rights.</p>

  <h2>Fees and payouts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>EasyNotes keeps <%= feePercent %>% of each sale price as its platform fee. You receive the rest.</li>
    <li>Payments are split by Paystack at the time of sale. Your share is settled to the bank account you provide, on Paystack’s settlement schedule.</li>
    <li>You are responsible for declaring your earnings to SARS.</li>
    <li>Sales are final for buyers. If we refund a buyer because a file was defective or misdescribed, the refunded amount may be recovered from future payouts.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>After you stop selling</h2>
  <p>If you unpublish notes, students who already bought them can still download them.</p>
</div>
<%- include('partials/bottom') %>
